# AI Clinic Assistant safety

Full spec: `docs/mvp.md` §9, `docs/architecture/ai-clinic-assistant.md`. Skill: `.agent/skills/ai-clinic-assistant/SKILL.md`.

## Three-tier model (server-computed, never model-decided)

| Tier | Meaning | Examples |
| ---- | ------- | -------- |
| **0 — read** | RBAC pass only; no writes | Patient lookup, today's appointments, balance check |
| **1 — auto** | Idempotent, low blast radius; visible "done" card | Mark thread read, benign status forward with no clinical/financial impact |
| **2 — confirm** | Proposal only until user taps Confirm | Cancel appointment, Rx, invoice line, patient message, SOAP edit, clinic settings |

## Always Tier 2 (override classifier)

- **Clinical writes**: SOAP, prescriptions, diagnoses — no exceptions.
- **External send**: any real message to a patient (reminder, summary, reschedule notice). Confirm button says **Send**, not generic Confirm.
- **Bulk**: 2+ writes in one turn → all Tier 2.
- **Cross-scope**: patient/appointment outside pinned context → Tier 2.

## Per-tool execution

1. Re-verify JWT + `clinic_memberships` role on every tool call — never trust model-supplied user or IDs.
2. Re-validate DB state immediately before Tier 1 writes; mismatch → hard fail, no write.
3. Log every executed write to `activity_log` with `actor_type: ai_assistant`.
4. Never build: silent patient sends, unconfirmed clinical writes, client-side tier override, PHI in tool debug logs.
